$HOME/alphazede/worktrees/amazon-fantasy-companion-planning/docs/plans/2026-10-11-amazon-fantasy-companion/implementation.json:3029:        "compared": "S06L lease 'harness-configs, alphazedehq-main-checkout' and S42 lease 'alphazedehq-main-checkout'. Both only read the checkout, and both dispatch on the S06 merge. Because DES-AFC-LANES grants each lease 'to one slice at a time', they serialize for no reason. Separately, 'fast-forward only, between dispatches' does not stop a fast-forward while Wave 1 or Wave 2 sessions run: under continuous dispatch, merges always land while other sessions are running. The S03 fast-forward changes ship-pull-request for every PR-opening session on the host.",
$HOME/alphazede/worktrees/amazon-fantasy-companion-planning/docs/plans/2026-10-11-amazon-fantasy-companion/implementation.json:3031:        "corrected_text": "- `alphazedehq-main-checkout`: a reader-writer lease. Slices that read skills from the checkout (S06L, S42) and the IE-P1-10 live install hold a shared read lease. The Orchestrator's fast-forward (CMD-AZHQ-SYNC) takes it exclusively. It runs only when no read lease is held and no session of this Lifecycle is opening or landing a pull request. Each sync records the HEAD before and after it and the sessions running at that moment. The HEAD is recorded in each later packet."
