$HOME/alphazede/worktrees/amazon-fantasy-companion-planning/docs/plans/2026-10-11-amazon-fantasy-companion/implementation.json:5241:        "evidence": "D4 form: extend the existing shared skills only (SD-018), or extend them and add one thin shared entry-point skill (the owner’s latest words were “Just create the shared skill please”). Recommendation: **A — extensions only.** `setup-pre-commit` becomes the shared CI/CD gate skill and is already linked into every harness. A second entry-point skill would only route to the three extended skills and duplicate their trigger surface, which C10 forbids. If “the shared skill” meant one new named skill, option B costs one judgement slice (S41, `skills/ci-cd/SKILL.md`, a router under 25 lines) and changes nothing else.",
$HOME/alphazede/worktrees/amazon-fantasy-companion-planning/docs/plans/2026-10-11-amazon-fantasy-companion/implementation.json:5271:        "evidence": "In a repository without a Vnv guidance tree, does `ship-pull-request`’s `REFUSED_NO_VNV` block the merge? Recommendation: No. Record it as a non-pass gate row (C12) and let the repository’s required checks decide. Blocking would stop merges in every repository the owner touches (SD-019). This repository has a tree, so it always runs `vnv-review`.",
$HOME/alphazede/worktrees/amazon-fantasy-companion-planning/docs/plans/2026-10-11-amazon-fantasy-companion/implementation.json:5277:        "evidence": "Lane for the D4/D5 skill-authoring slices (S01, S02, S03, S06). **A:** spec-and-docs = tech-writing profile (single_implementer; Reviewer with OCR still applies). **B:** keep SKILL.md and references text on tech-writing, and move the executable parts (gate template, hook installer, workflow checker, D5 scripts) to the primary profile with tdd. Recommendation: **A** for the schedule. B’s risk stays visible: the executable shared tooling gets no Assurance Test Engineer pass, only the Reviewer and the scripts’ own tests. Phase 1 has more slack than f885e48 had, so B is now affordable: it costs about one day and a slice-graph/SEIT regeneration.",
