type: reference
title: Pull Request Body Contract
okf_status: active
tags:
  - internal
  - operations
---

# Pull Request Body Contract

Four sections, in this order. A missing section is a blocked PR.

```markdown
## What changed

- One bullet per externally visible change, imperative mood.
- Name the invariant a change establishes, not the files it touched.

## Why

The property that did not hold before and holds now. State the constraint the
change was built under when one shaped the design.

## Validation

- Each command exactly as run, one per line.
- The result: counts, exit status, what the output showed.

## Residual risk

- Every gate not run, and why.
- Every accepted limitation of the approach.
- `no known gap` only when that is literally true.
```

## Rules

- Validation lists commands actually run in this branch. A command you intend
  to run belongs under Residual risk until it has run.
- An unavailable environment is a residual risk, not an omission. Name the
  missing configuration.
- This body is the permanent review record for the change. Rebase-merge keeps
  the individual commit messages, so the body is not the commit message. Write
  both to be read a year later by someone bisecting.
- When creating or editing PR descriptions, never use `gh pr edit` (on Ubuntu
  `gh 2.45.0`, it fails on the deprecated Projects-classic GraphQL schema and
  silently leaves text stale). Always update using GitHub REST PATCH
  (`gh api -X PATCH repos/<owner>/<repo>/pulls/<n> -F body=@<file>` or
  `scripts/edit-pr.sh`) and perform the verification
  readback (`gh api repos/<owner>/<repo>/pulls/<n> --jq '{title: .title, body: .body}'`
  or `scripts/check-pr-text.sh`) to detect and reject stale PR text.

## Worked example

`alphazede/bran-dev#14` states its gate output (`--fast`, 263 core and 38 CLI
tests) and discloses that the live external-host smoke test could not run
because the required environment configuration was unavailable, and that the
PR therefore stays draft. That disclosure is the pattern to copy.
#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Validate the skill and check independent forward-test classifications.

Set RELEASE_TRIGGER_RESULTS to the evaluator's JSON (case id -> MATCH/NO_MATCH).
Give the evaluator SKILL.md and trigger-requests.json without this checker.
"""

import json
import os
from pathlib import Path
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile
import unittest

import yaml


SKILL = Path(os.environ.get("RELEASE_SKILL_DIR", Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]))
CREATOR = Path.home() / ".codex/skills/.system/skill-creator/scripts/quick_validate.py"


class ReleaseProcessTests(unittest.TestCase):
    def test_creator_validation_and_repository_metadata(self):
        text = (SKILL / "SKILL.md").read_text()
        self.assertLess(len(text.splitlines()), 60)
        self.assertLess(len(text.split()), 400)
        _, header, body = text.split("---", 2)
        metadata = yaml.safe_load(header)
        self.assertEqual(metadata["name"], "release-process")
        for field in ("type", "title", "okf_status", "tags"):
            self.assertTrue(metadata[field], field)
        # The installed validator rejects HQ metadata. Validate its portable
        # fields unchanged; BRAN validates the complete repository document.
        portable = {key: value for key, value in metadata.items() if key in
                    {"name", "description", "license", "allowed-tools", "metadata"}}
        with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as target:
            Path(target, "SKILL.md").write_text(
                "---\n" + yaml.safe_dump(portable) + "---" + body)
            subprocess.run([sys.executable, str(CREATOR), target], check=True)

    def test_trigger_classifications(self):
        requests = json.loads((Path(__file__).parent / "trigger-requests.json").read_text())
        results = json.loads(Path(os.environ["RELEASE_TRIGGER_RESULTS"]).read_text())
        self.assertEqual(set(results), set(requests))
        self.assertEqual(results, {"request_1": "MATCH", "request_2": "NO_MATCH"})


if __name__ == "__main__":
    unittest.main()
{
  "request_1": "cut a release of alphazede/azedge",
  "request_2": "open a PR"
}
