# Release Process

## Procedure

1. Resolve the target checkout and push remote; read its AGENTS, CONTRIBUTING,
   manifests, release workflows, and scripts. Use repository tools, git, gh,
   registry and signature verifiers. Honor checkout and credential rules.
2. Record repository, previous/new version, source commit, tag, version files,
   gates, publish trigger, expected artifacts/signatures, notes, consumers,
   and authority. Distinguish registry/manual dispatch from tag-triggered
   publication. Missing or conflicting evidence means `NEEDS_EVIDENCE`.
   For Bearing Lite read [npm details](references/BEARING-LITE.md); for BRAN
   read [publish-bran](../publish-bran/SKILL.md).
   For notes/pins only, verify the existing release; skip versioning and
   new publication.
3. Apply repository version policy across every manifest and lockfile.
   Run workflow-equivalent local gates, artifact dry runs, security checks,
   and required smoke tests. Red checks, open alerts, or untested required
   hosts block publication. Land changes through `$ship-pull-request`;
   confirm the merged source is green.
4. Prepare artifacts and notes before requesting missing authorization.
   Require current-session owner instruction naming the repository/release
   before irreversible publication, including notes and release-triggering
   tags. Existing instruction suffices; never infer it from green main.
5. Recheck remote, merged commit, versions, and local/remote tag and registry
   absence. Never reuse or force-push tags or republish immutable versions.
   Run only the discovered publisher. Never approve environment jobs;
   return `WAITING_ON` with the run URL and resume from observed state.
6. Verify workflow completion and downloaded/registry artifact identity,
   contents, checksums, and required signatures against the expected source.
   Publish/read back notes using [format](references/RELEASE-NOTES.md).
7. Before merging consumer re-pins, run `scripts/find-pin-consumers.sh
   [OLD_SHA256] OLD_VERSION WORKSPACE` for outgoing pins; empty digest
   means version-only. Classify every hit;
   update authorized live guards/pins together, retain historical evidence.
   Exit 2 or live old pins block merge. Gate pin PRs; installation/activation
   needs separate authority. Confirm propagation; clean temporary checkouts
   only after merged proof and no live references.

## Recovery and result

Allow three evidence-driven corrections; stop without new evidence. Never
retry a publisher blindly: reconcile registry, tags, releases, and run state.
Return `PUBLISHED` only after artifacts, notes, and required consumers verify;
otherwise `BLOCKED`, `WAITING_ON`, `NEEDS_OWNER_DECISION`, or `NEEDS_EVIDENCE`.
Include repository/version/tag/source, run URL, checks, pins, and exact gaps.

